    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="The double pendulum is a simple mechanical system -- two point masses m_1, m_2 on massless rigid rods of length l_1, l_2, hanging from a fixed pivot under gravity g, with no friction -- whose motion is nonetheless chaotic for large enough swings. In terms of the two rod angles \theta_1, \theta_2 from vertical and their angular velocities \omega_1 = \dot\theta_1, \omega_2 = \dot\theta_2, the equations of motion are">

.. only:: html

